      "description": "The tangential inlet sets up a swirl. Dense sand grains are thrown outward to the wall and slide down into the cone, while the cleaned fluid turns and leaves through the central vortex finder. Sand removal protects chokes, valves and separators from erosion. The rising ΔP / sand level triggers a dump (flush) of the cone — always under controlled conditions because of the erosive, pressurised discharge.",
